-- handleTelegramUpdate — entry point invoked by the webhook route per
-- inbound Telegram update.
--
-- Two parallel pipelines fan out from each update:
--
--   1. The COLLECTOR dispatch (stepConversation) — pattern-matches on
--      the typed Update + the typed ConversationStatus to route
--      through any active form-fill conversation, the confirmation
--      step, /start collector autostart, and callback_query button
--      dispatch.
--   2. The USER-TRIGGER dispatch (dispatchEventTriggers) — fans the
--      event out to every user-defined function whose trigger
--      matches.
--
-- The collector dispatch runs first so an active form-fill claims its
-- own messages (one reply per inbound message) before user triggers
-- get a shot. This keeps the collector's UX coherent in the presence
-- of conflicting user triggers.
--
-- Phase 11c sub-step 3 — the body now calls stepConversation directly
-- with the typed Update (no intermediate flat-payload shim). The
-- minimal flatPayloadForTriggers helper preserves the user-trigger
-- payload contract (Decision EE — conservative back-compat; full
-- contract change deferred to a future workstream).
--
-- Decode failure (Err) is logged + the update is silently dropped per
-- Decision GG (don't NACK Telegram on schema drift; the log is the
-- monitoring surface).
--
-- module-substrate Phase 3o (2026-05-31) — migrated to `module telegram where`.
-- The defineFunction spec + HANDLE_UPDATE_BODY extraction RETIRED; identity rides
-- @facet directives. Def head renamed handleTelegramUpdate → handleUpdate with
-- @codeName preserving the public codeName (poll's dispatchOnePollingUpdate +
-- the webhook route resolve `handleTelegramUpdate` by codeName). `requires`
-- INFERRED. Body UNCHANGED.

module telegram where

@label "Handle Telegram Update"
@description "Dispatch one inbound Telegram update for a registered bot. The webhook route invokes this when Telegram posts an update; the body decodes the JsonValue payload into the typed Update ADT then routes it through stepConversation (collector form-fill engine — start/confirm/field/picker handlers) and through any user-defined function triggers via dispatchEventTriggers. This is the lifecycle function — it runs once per inbound update."
@tags "telegram" "collector" "io" "lifecycle"
@icon "inbox"
@emoji "📨"
@ioAction "telegram_collector.handle_update"
@codeName "handleTelegramUpdate"
handleUpdate : (botId: BotId) -> (updateJson: JsonValue) -> (accountId: String) -> Unit
handleUpdate botId updateJson accountId =
  let wrapped = wrapJsonValue updateJson
  case decodeUpdate wrapped of
    Err _e -> 0
    Ok update ->
      stepConversation botId update accountId
      let flat = flatPayloadForTriggers botId update
      dispatchEventTriggers flat.eventType flat.payload
